The desk merged every date report into #4471 and marked it known, with one fix queued. The
reports hold more than one problem. This page splits them. The tickets are in the
[project issues](https://github.com/franProton100/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues).

<Callout kind="warn">
Counts are from the export of 4 October. The desk keeps working, so live numbers may differ.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemCounts ticket={4471} leftIn={['R-41236']} />

1. **Month and day swapped.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Tenants that write
   the day first get flipped dates. Ticket
   [#1](https://github.com/franProton100/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
2. **Form hint.** Day-first tenants on the booking-v3 form see an MM/DD hint, so people type month
   first. This needs a different fix from the parser. Ticket
   [#2](https://github.com/franProton100/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).
3. **One day off.** Four reports show a date one day off in the same month. A month swap cannot
   make that. The cause is not known. Ticket
   [#3](https://github.com/franProton100/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3).

## How the reports were sorted

- One id is one report. The export overlaps, so repeats are removed first.
- A report's cause comes from its **tenant** (the locale it writes dates in, and its booking
  form), not from the subject line. The desk merged by subject, and that is how three problems
  became one ticket.
- The **intake tag** is a guess from the reporter's browser. It is shown for comparison and is
  never used to sort.
- The desk's own table below counts the five desk-flagged one-day reports under the shared parser.
  This page separates four of them (R-41236 is explained at the end), so its parser count is
  smaller. The table also predates tickets 1 to 3, so its "no ticket of its own" note is out of
  date.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What we do not know

<Callout>
The cause of the one-day reports is unconfirmed. One reporter says only June is affected. That is
not checked against other reports. The form hint cause comes from tenant and form data. The
reports' own text never mentions the form.
</Callout>

One desk-flagged report, R-41236, says an invite arrived before the booking was made. It describes
no day shift, so it stays under the shared parser.

